  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Account for the power outside the brackets",
      "body": "<p>The whole expression has a factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> outside. To obtain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></math> overall, find the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> term inside the expansion.</p>",
      "recap": "Include outside factors when choosing the required exponent.",
      "pitfall": "Looking for the fourth power inside would give the sixth power overall.",
      "pause": "Find how many reciprocal terms are needed inside.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b2-l05",
          "reminder": "Include outside factors when choosing the required exponent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Count the exponent supplied by each choice",
      "body": "<p>Choose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> from k of the six brackets and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> from the other <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math>. The power inside is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Add all positive and negative exponent contributions.",
      "pitfall": "Changing a selection from x to its reciprocal reduces the total exponent by two.",
      "pause": "Find k, then count the ways of making those choices.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l11",
          "reminder": "Add all positive and negative exponent contributions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Count the contributing selections",
      "body": "Use your value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></math> to count which factors supplied the reciprocal term. Then include the numerical coefficient from every remaining factor.",
      "recap": "A binomial coefficient counts selections, not the entire term coefficient.",
      "pitfall": "The outer factor changes the power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, but does not create extra selections.",
      "pause": "Calculate the coefficient and compare it with the options.",
      "recall": [
