  "solution": "<p><strong>1. Remove the outside exponent from the target.</strong> The required term inside is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2. Select the correct factors.</strong> Choosing two reciprocal terms and four <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> terms gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3. Calculate the coefficient.</strong> This is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#x000D7;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>240</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer E.</strong> The outside factor changes the target exponent, not the numerical coefficient.</p>",
